    "every build type (standard, risky, design, large, ui, research, rca, chore)": "use the build list in order, led per type by `leads` and limited by `only`: the `router` entry runs the Morph chain its `routes` table names for the type (every type runs DeepSeek V4.1 Flash then DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017, which has its own Morph budget; Kimi K3.1 is out because its 24,290 uncached tokens a minute is smaller than one fresh pi request), then Cursor auto, then Terra for quick, chore, standard, ui and research or Sol for rca, risky, design and hard",
    "fix and finish rounds": "use the fix list in order: the `router` entry on its standard chain, Cursor auto, Sol at max reasoning",
    "reviewer vendor must differ from the builder's executed vendor": "skip review entries of the same vendor; reviews are Astra then Opus",
    "a provider that fails with no credits, usage limit or auth": "is skipped for all callers until its hourly probe answers",
    "builder:<id> label": "tries that entry first, then the list",
    "panel": "runs only when Shyam asks for one (Fable on request); nothing starts a panel on its own",
    "never": "OpenAI API models (instance openai-api) as builders"
  }
